&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="font-family: Arial;"&gt;In conjunction with certain derivative contracts, we are required to provide collateral to and receive collateral from our counterparty through restricted cash deposits placed in margin accounts. As of June 30, 2026, we had a cash margin of $3 million posted by our counterparty with us as collateral and reported within Account 242 "Miscellaneous Current and Accrued Liabilities" on our balance sheet. As of June 30, 2026 and December 31, 2025, we had a cash margin deposit of $1 million posted with our counterparty and recorded in Account 134 &amp;#8220;Other Special Deposits&amp;#8221; on our balance sheet.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-bottom: 0pt; text-align: justify; font-size: 16pt;"&gt;&lt;font style="-aw-import: ignore;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
